From 25a74d096fbf633bbaa408accf5fb3bfefba760c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (review)" <review@localhost>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:38:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Stage 2b: durable submission ownership, end-to-end submit
 budget, lock release off

- post_inflight marker set in the intent-creating transaction and cleared only
  by the POST worker when the request ends; visible to all gateways/processes;
  survives owner crash (no lease/expiry treated as proof). Abandon/release
  refuse while set, or after an 'ok:' POST outcome.
- One monotonic Budget carries submit_deadline_s through POST wait, DB writes
  (sqlite busy timeout capped to remaining), reconcile reads and scan pages;
  exhausted -> UNRESOLVED, reconcile deferred.
- LOCK_RELEASE_ENABLED=False: operational lock release disabled; mechanism
  tests opt in explicitly (make3, make3b, round-3b gateway()).
- Worker bookkeeping writes ownership columns only (no state/history), keeping
  the stage-2 late-completion invariant.

Tests: stage2b 8 (8 fail on b228258; 8 pass); all 103 pass; stable across
combined, repeated and reversed runs. Codex reviewer_checks.py verbatim:
abandon refused, lock held, 0.05 s budget -> 0.016 s UNRESOLVED.
